# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone would otherwise hand them CRLF, and a
# bash script with CRLF fails at the shebang — `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env
# bash^M` — which is a confusing first thing for a self-hoster to hit when
# running scripts/setup.sh under WSL or Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
